From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Sun, 23 Apr 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: require empty opposing team fields for Tag direct
 attacks

Owner decision 2026-10-07 and Konami Tag Attacking: either opposing duelist MMZ or EMZ blocks an ordinary direct attack. Sum only the opposing monster counts, keeping SELF_ATTACK partner targets from blocking it. Targets still include both opponents. Explicit direct-attack effects, FFA and 1v1 behavior remain unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019EpX1AcvnigK9dTsxAa5W9
---
 field.cpp | 10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/field.cpp b/field.cpp
index ee3fd2d..241f982 100644
--- a/field.cpp
+++ b/field.cpp
@@ -3456,13 +3456,17 @@ int32_t field::get_attack_target(card* pcard, card_vector* v, bool chain_attack,
 	}
 	if(atype <= 3)
 		return atype;
-	// With more than 2 duelists the direct attack can go to every living opponent that has no monster
-	// (to all of them with EFFECT_DIRECT_ATTACK or core.attack_player). The mask has one bit per duelist.
+	// FFA checks each defender. Tag checks the combined opposing monster fields
+	// (MMZ and EMZ); card-granted direct attacks keep their stock exception.
+	// The direct attack mask has one bit per opposing duelist.
 	uint32_t dmask = 0;
 	if(n_duelists > 2) {
 		const bool any_side = pcard->is_affected_by_effect(EFFECT_DIRECT_ATTACK) || core.attack_player;
+		uint32_t opposing_mcount = 0;
 		for(uint8_t oi = 0; oi < opp_count; ++oi)
-			if((any_side || mcount_by[opps[oi]] == 0)
+			opposing_mcount += mcount_by[opps[oi]];
+		for(uint8_t oi = 0; oi < opp_count; ++oi)
+			if((any_side || (n_teams == 2 ? opposing_mcount : mcount_by[opps[oi]]) == 0)
 				&& (n_teams != n_duelists || !is_player_affected_by_effect(opps[oi], EFFECT_CANNOT_BE_DIRECT_ATTACKED)))
 				dmask |= 1u << opps[oi];
 	}
